2.0.0
- Major workflow release for Miner's Blueprint
- Expanded the mod from a selection/copy-paste helper into a broader building and world-editing toolkit
- Added blueprint import/export, build modes, transforms, remove/cut workflows, undo, selection editing, improved notifications, and richer Chat Commands integration
- Curated `/help mb` output while preserving dynamic autocomplete through the updated Chat Commands API

1.1.0
- Added blueprint export/import:
  - `/mb export selection <FileName>` saves the current copied clipboard to `FileName.blueprint`
  - `/mb export all <FileName>` saves all supported saveable world objects to `FileName.blueprint`
  - `/mb import <FileName>` loads a `.blueprint` file back into the runtime clipboard and opens the ghost preview
- Added build mode switching:
  - `/mb mode normal` keeps inventory-gated placement
  - `/mb mode unlimited` bypasses inventory checks and item consumption
- Added disk-backed `.blueprint` sharing files under `BepInEx/config/MinersBlueprint/Blueprints`
- Added world-anchored import behavior for `all` exports so they restore to the saved world position instead of the player position
- Reworked action notifications into compact top-right popups with a quick fade-out
- Fixed Chat Commands registration to use the correct `com.ChatCommands` plugin GUID
- Added dynamic `/mb` autocomplete entries for discovered blueprint file names
- Added exact blueprint path/directory reporting in export/import/list/rename flows
- Added blueprint management commands:
  - `/mb blueprints list`
  - `/mb blueprints rename <CurrentFileName> <NewFileName>`
  - `/mb blueprints delete <CurrentFileName>`
  - `/mb confirm`
- Added undo support for the latest paste/removal action:
  - `/mb undo [Count]`
- Changed paste to use adaptive staged slices on the axis with the largest span, with a `0.1s` delay between slices
- Normalized the primary command surface:
  - `/mb place`
  - `/mb clear clipboard|ghost|selection|all`
  - `/mb blueprints save selection|all`
  - `/mb blueprints import`
  - `/mb pos`
  - `/mb size`
  - direction aliases `n/s/e/w/u/d`
- Added a tagged `/mb tool` pickaxe:
  - left click sets pos1
  - right click sets pos2
  - middle click copies the current selection
- Added green outline highlights for objects inside a completed selection
- Removed placement animation experiments; staged placement is timing-only
- Added support for selecting, exporting, importing, cutting, and removing supported saveable world items beyond buildings:
  - tools
  - pumpkins / `JackOLantern`
  - sleds
  - boxes
  - similar `ISaveLoadableObject` world items
- Added selection/world editing commands:
  - `/mb cut`
  - `/mb remove`
  - `/mb shift <Direction> <Amount>`
  - `/mb grow <Amount>`
  - `/mb shrink <Amount>`
  - `/mb expand <Direction> <Amount>`
  - `/mb contract <Direction> <Amount>`
- Added clipboard transform commands:
  - `/mb rotate 90`
  - `/mb rotate 180`
  - `/mb rotate 270`
  - `/mb mirror`
  - `/mb stack <Count> <Direction> <Gap>`
- Improved build metadata hygiene:
  - version metadata aligned across `ModInfo.cs`, `.csproj`, docs
  - build path override support via `MineMogulDir`, `MINE_MOGUL_DIR`, `MineMogulInstallDir`
  - validation for MineMogul/BepInEx reference paths
  - removed stale Harmony/Input System dependency drift
- Refreshed `DirectoryOverview.md` so a new AI session can reconstruct the current project state from files alone

0.1.1
- Initial release as Miner's Blueprint
- Added 3D selection flow:
  - Key 1 sets start point from looked object/hit position
  - Key 2 sets end point and builds a green world-space selection box
- Added optional debug window listing objects in current selection and clipboard counts
- Added clipboard copy/paste:
  - Key 3 copies placed building objects in selection
  - Key 4 pastes copied objects relative to player position
- Added variant-aware paste support
- Added inventory gate on paste:
  - requires matching building items (`ToolBuilder` stacks) in inventory
  - blocks paste if missing items and shows exact missing counts
  - consumes required items from inventory when paste succeeds
